0..73 Comment "//! A fold over a type whose rule swaps two variables respects that rule."
74..77 Comment "//!"
78..156 Comment "//! Two purses in one purse have no order, and the rule of the purse swaps its"
157..232 Comment "//! two variables. A fold reads each field by a call of its own. So the two"
233..293 Comment "//! sides of the rule hold the same two calls in two orders."
294..297 Comment "//!"
298..372 Comment "//! The check reads the call of the fold at each variable of a rule as one"
373..451 Comment "//! value. The two sides then differ by the order of two fields alone, and the"
452..530 Comment "//! rule joins them. The kernel decides the fold again by its own code, and it"
531..574 Comment "//! searches the pairing of the two fields."
575..578 Comment "//!"
579..651 Comment "//! A call that gives a purse in one order equals the purse in the other"
652..725 Comment "//! order. The checker names the crossed pairing of the two fields at the"
726..799 Comment "//! value that the call returns, and the kernel replays it at that value."
800..803 Comment "//!"
804..820 Comment "//! - see: #8367"
821..837 Comment "//! - see: #8385"
838..915 Comment "//! - see: `pathological/desc/fold-swaps-variables.gandr` — a fold that the"
916..934 Comment "//!   rule refuses"
935..1012 Comment "//! - see: `model/desc/fold-drops-variable.gandr` — a fold over a rule that"
1013..1035 Comment "//!   drops a variable"
